// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 12-type-system
// facility: rule.type.eq [Eq-Struct] (a `StringView` payload is a slice, which has no equality, D-0047); conf.view-in-aggregate-eq (CHG-0276)
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// Two views compare by their text (D-0053), but `[Eq-Struct]` compares an
// `Option<StringView>` by its payload's fields, and a view's field is a
// slice. Compare the payloads: `Option::unwrap(a) == "x"`, or a `match`.

import std;

fn main()
{
    Option<StringView> a = Some(StringView::of("x"));
    assert(a == Some(StringView::of("x")));
}
